---
import data from '../data/generated/core_analysis_summary.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const model = data.adjusted_model;
const regressionFigure = `${base.replace(/\/$/, '')}/images/analysis/02_adjusted_imd_score_predictions.png`;
---

<section class="exposure-model" aria-labelledby="exposure-model-title">
	<header class="exposure-model-heading">
		<div>
			<p class="method-label">Adjusted regression</p>
			<h3 id="exposure-model-title">A common adjustment structure is applied to three exposure measures.</h3>
		</div>
		<p>Continuous IMD score is modelled non-linearly. Rural–urban class, population density and region are held in the same specification for count, density and share.</p>
	</header>

	<div class="regression-specification">
		<div
			class="regression-equation"
			role="math"
			aria-label="Outcome-specific link of expected exposure equals an intercept, a spline of IMD score, rural urban class, log population density and region"
		>
			<span><i>g</i><sub>k</sub>(E[<i>Y</i><sub>ik</sub> | <i>X</i><sub>i</sub>])</span>
			<b>=</b>
			<span><i>β</i><sub>0k</sub> + <i>s</i><sub>k</sub>(IMD<sub>i</sub>) + <i>γ</i><sub>k</sub>RUC<sub>i</sub> + <i>β</i><sub>1k</sub>log(1 + population density<sub>i</sub>) + <i>δ</i><sub>k</sub>region<sub>i</sub></span>
		</div>
		<div class="regression-equation-note">
			<p><i>i</i> indexes England LSOAs and <i>k</i> indexes the three exposure outcomes. <i>s</i><sub>k</sub>(IMD) is a restricted cubic spline with four degrees of freedom; RUC 2021 and region enter as categorical terms, and population density is log-transformed.</p>
			<p>The outcome-specific link <i>g</i><sub>k</sub> is log for the negative-binomial count model, identity for OLS on log(1 + density), and logit for the fractional-share model.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="regression-model-grid">
			{model.models.map((entry) => (
				<article>
					<strong>{entry.outcome}</strong>
					<span>{entry.family}</span>
					<small>{entry.link} link · n = {entry.n.toLocaleString('en-GB')}</small>
				</article>
			))}
		</div>

		<p class="regression-meta">{model.covariance} covariance · {(model.confidence_level * 100).toFixed(0)}% confidence intervals · predictions across the {model.imd_range}</p>
	</div>

	<figure class="regression-figure" aria-labelledby="regression-figure-title">
		<div class="regression-figure-heading">
			<div>
				<p class="method-label">Conditional association</p>
				<h3 id="regression-figure-title">Adjusted fast-food exposure across the continuous IMD score</h3>
			</div>
			<p>Higher IMD scores indicate greater deprivation. Predictions hold RUC at {model.reference_profile.ruc21nm}, region at {model.reference_profile.region22nm}, and population density at the {model.reference_profile.population_density.toLowerCase()}.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="regression-image-frame">
			<img
				src={regressionFigure}
				alt="Three adjusted regression curves for fast-food restaurant count, population-standardised density and fast-food share across the continuous IMD score. Each curve includes a shaded 95% confidence interval."
				loading="lazy"
			/>
		</div>

		<figcaption>Lines are model-predicted values; shaded ribbons are robust 95% confidence intervals. The curves describe conditional area-level associations and do not identify platform targeting, ordering or consumption.</figcaption>
	</figure>
</section>
